# Slice 290 (U3, a part root's field as a hidden input): methods of the program part part_root_hidden_part.lm2 use the free
# name `scale`, whose lexical source is the field of the part's root, called from outside the part.  The book :687, :773,
# :775: a free name takes an admissible dynamic input first, then its lexical source, held at the activation's entry; a bare
# write changes only the activation's value (Q52; :691, :775); `node\scale` writes the root's field (:789).  On the 289 tuple
# the native read failed `walk error: INVALID` (the place of the absent input got no type) and under --walk-methods the
# write-only set_scale threw `implements` (its source was never held).  Entry 7; 11.. name the failing check.
fn: shadowed () int
    int: scale 9
    return: part_scale()
end: shadowed
fn: shadow_set () int
